2. MATCH CORE IsUnspendable UTXO SEMANTICS
===========================================

Qogecoin Core CCoinsViewCache::AddCoin does:

  if (coin.out.scriptPubKey.IsUnspendable()) return;

Core's CScript::IsUnspendable() is exactly:

  (size() > 0 && first opcode == OP_RETURN)
  OR
  size() > MAX_SCRIPT_SIZE

where:

  MAX_SCRIPT_SIZE = 10000

Therefore transaction_outputs and utxo_state have DIFFERENT cardinality.

transaction_outputs:
  preserve EVERY output 1:1 forever

utxo_state:
  represent only outputs Core would actually add to its coins view

Implement a small, exact structural helper mirroring Core semantics.

Prefer putting it somewhere appropriate in internal/script, e.g.:

  IsUnspendable(script []byte) bool

with behavior equivalent to Core:

  len(script) > 0 && script[0] == OP_RETURN
  ||
  len(script) > 10000

Do not substitute:

  ScriptType == nulldata

because Core's rule is based on raw script bytes and also includes scripts
larger than MAX_SCRIPT_SIZE.

In applyOutput:

- ALWAYS persist transaction_outputs
- persist display/search metadata normally
- create utxo_state ONLY if:
    - block is not genesis
    - ScriptPubKey is NOT Core-IsUnspendable

An unspendable output is not a missing transaction output.
It is an immutable output that deliberately has no canonical coin/UTXO row.


